\mt1 Joel  
\c 2  
\p
\v 1 \w Blow\w* ye the \w trumpet\w* in \w Zion\w*, and sound an \w alarm\w* in my \w holy\w* \w mountain\w*: let all the \w inhabitants\w* of the \w land\w* \w tremble\w*: for the \w day\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \w cometh\w*, for \add it is\add* nigh at \w hand\w*;\f + \fr 2.1 \ft trumpet: or, cornet\f*  
\v 2 A \w day\w* of \w darkness\w* and of \w gloominess\w*, a \w day\w* of \w clouds\w* and of thick \w darkness\w*, as the \w morning\w* \w spread\w* upon the \w mountains\w*: a \w great\w* \w people\w* and a \w strong\w*; there hath not \w been\w* \w ever\w* the like, neither shall be any \w more\w* \w after\w* it, \add even\add* to the \w years\w* of \w many\w* \w generations\w*.\f + \fr 2.2 \ft of many…: Heb. of generation and generation\f*  
\v 3 A \w fire\w* \w devoureth\w* \w before\w* them; and \w behind\w* them a \w flame\w* \w burneth\w*: the \w land\w* \add is\add* as the \w garden\w* of \w Eden\w* \w before\w* them, and \w behind\w* them a \w desolate\w* \w wilderness\w*; yea, and nothing shall \w escape\w* them.  
\v 4 The \w appearance\w* of them \add is\add* as the \w appearance\w* of \w horses\w*; and as \w horsemen\w*, so shall they \w run\w*.  
\v 5 Like the \w noise\w* of \w chariots\w* on the \w tops\w* of \w mountains\w* shall they \w leap\w*, like the \w noise\w* of a \w flame\w* of \w fire\w* that \w devoureth\w* the \w stubble\w*, as a \w strong\w* \w people\w* set in \w battle\w* \w array\w*.  
\v 6 Before their \w face\w* the \w people\w* shall be much \w pained\w*: all \w faces\w* shall \w gather\w* \w blackness\w*.\f + \fr 2.6 \ft blackness: Heb. pot\f*  
\v 7 They shall \w run\w* like mighty \w men\w*; they shall \w climb\w* the \w wall\w* like \w men\w* of \w war\w*; and they shall \w march\w* every \w one\w* on his \w ways\w*, and they shall not \w break\w* their \w ranks\w*:  
\v 8 Neither shall \w one\w* \w thrust\w* \w another\w*; they shall \w walk\w* every \w one\w* in his \w path\w*: and \add when\add* they \w fall\w* upon the \w sword\w*, they shall not be \w wounded\w*.\f + \fr 2.8 \ft sword: or, dart\f*  
\v 9 They shall run to and \w fro\w* in the \w city\w*; they shall \w run\w* upon the \w wall\w*, they shall climb \w up\w* upon the \w houses\w*; they shall enter \w in\w* at the \w windows\w* like a \w thief\w*.  
\v 10 The \w earth\w* shall \w quake\w* \w before\w* them; the \w heavens\w* shall \w tremble\w*: the \w sun\w* and the \w moon\w* shall be \w dark\w*, and the \w stars\w* shall \w withdraw\w* their \w shining\w*:  
\v 11 And the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* shall \w utter\w* his \w voice\w* \w before\w* his \w army\w*: for his \w camp\w* \add is\add* \w very\w* \w great\w*: for \add he is\add* \w strong\w* that \w executeth\w* his \w word\w*: for the \w day\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \add is\add* \w great\w* and \w very\w* \w terrible\w*; and who can \w abide\w* it?   
\p
\v 12 ¶ Therefore also now, \w saith\w* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*, \w turn\w* ye \add even\add* to me with all your \w heart\w*, and with \w fasting\w*, and with \w weeping\w*, and with \w mourning\w*:  
\v 13 And \w rend\w* your \w heart\w*, and not your \w garments\w*, and \w turn\w* unto the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* your \w God\w*: for he \add is\add* \w gracious\w* and \w merciful\w*, \w slow\w* to \w anger\w*, and of \w great\w* \w kindness\w*, and \w repenteth\w* him of the \w evil\w*.  
\v 14 Who \w knoweth\w* \add if\add* he will \w return\w* and \w repent\w*, and \w leave\w* a \w blessing\w* \w behind\w* him; \add even\add* a meat \w offering\w* and a drink \w offering\w* unto the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* your \w God\w*?   
\p
\v 15 ¶ \w Blow\w* the \w trumpet\w* in \w Zion\w*, \w sanctify\w* a \w fast\w*, \w call\w* a solemn \w assembly\w*:  
\v 16 \w Gather\w* the \w people\w*, \w sanctify\w* the \w congregation\w*, \w assemble\w* the \w elders\w*, \w gather\w* the \w children\w*, and those that \w suck\w* the \w breasts\w*: let the \w bridegroom\w* go \w forth\w* of his \w chamber\w*, and the \w bride\w* out of her \w closet\w*.  
\v 17 Let the \w priests\w*, the \w ministers\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*, \w weep\w* between the \w porch\w* and the \w altar\w*, and let them \w say\w*, \w Spare\w* thy \w people\w*, O \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*, and \w give\w* not thine \w heritage\w* to \w reproach\w*, that the \w heathen\w* should rule \w over\w* them: wherefore should they \w say\w* among the \w people\w*, Where \add is\add* their \w God\w*?\f + \fr 2.17 \ft rule over: or, use a byword against\f*   
\p
\v 18 ¶ Then will the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* be \w jealous\w* for his \w land\w*, and \w pity\w* his \w people\w*.  
\v 19 Yea, the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* will \w answer\w* and \w say\w* unto his \w people\w*, Behold, I will \w send\w* you \w corn\w*, and \w wine\w*, and \w oil\w*, and ye shall be \w satisfied\w* therewith: and I will no more \w make\w* you a \w reproach\w* among the \w heathen\w*:  
\v 20 But I will remove far \w off\w* from you the \w northern\w* \add army\add*, and will \w drive\w* him into a \w land\w* \w barren\w* and \w desolate\w*, with his \w face\w* toward the \w east\w* \w sea\w*, and his hinder \w part\w* toward the \w utmost\w* \w sea\w*, and his \w stink\w* shall come \w up\w*, and his ill \w savour\w* shall come \w up\w*, because he hath \w done\w* great \w things\w*.\f + \fr 2.20 \ft hath…: Heb. hath magnified to do\f*   
\p
\v 21 ¶ \w Fear\w* not, O \w land\w*; be \w glad\w* and \w rejoice\w*: for the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* will \w do\w* great \w things\w*.\f + \fr 2.21 \ft will…: Heb. hath magnified to do\f*  
\v 22 Be not \w afraid\w*, ye \w beasts\w* of the \w field\w*: for the \w pastures\w* of the \w wilderness\w* do \w spring\w*, for the \w tree\w* \w beareth\w* her \w fruit\w*, the fig \w tree\w* and the \w vine\w* do \w yield\w* their \w strength\w*.  
\v 23 Be \w glad\w* then, ye \w children\w* of \w Zion\w*, and \w rejoice\w* in the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* your \w God\w*: for he hath \w given\w* you the former \w rain\w* \w moderately\w*, and he will cause to come \w down\w* for you the \w rain\w*, the former \w rain\w*, and the latter \w rain\w* in the \w first\w* \add month\add*.\f + \fr 2.23 \ft the former rain moderately: or, a teacher of righteousness\f*\f + \fr 2.23 \ft moderately: Heb. according to righteousness\f*  
\v 24 And the \w floors\w* shall be \w full\w* of \w wheat\w*, and the \w fats\w* shall \w overflow\w* with \w wine\w* and \w oil\w*.  
\v 25 And I will \w restore\w* to you the \w years\w* that the \w locust\w* hath \w eaten\w*, the \w cankerworm\w*, and the \w caterpiller\w*, and the \w palmerworm\w*, my \w great\w* \w army\w* which I \w sent\w* among you.  
\v 26 And ye shall \w eat\w* in \w plenty\w*, and be \w satisfied\w*, and \w praise\w* the \w name\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* your \w God\w*, that hath \w dealt\w* \w wondrously\w* with you: and my \w people\w* shall \w never\w* be \w ashamed\w*.  
\v 27 And ye shall \w know\w* that I \add am\add* in the \w midst\w* of \w Israel\w*, and \add that\add* I \add am\add* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* your \w God\w*, and none else: and my \w people\w* shall \w never\w* be \w ashamed\w*.   
\p
\v 28 ¶ And it shall come to pass \w afterward\w*, \add that\add* I will pour \w out\w* my \w spirit\w* upon all \w flesh\w*; and your \w sons\w* and your \w daughters\w* shall \w prophesy\w*, your old \w men\w* shall \w dream\w* \w dreams\w*, your young \w men\w* shall \w see\w* \w visions\w*:  
\v 29 And also upon the \w servants\w* and upon the \w handmaids\w* in those \w days\w* will I pour \w out\w* my \w spirit\w*.  
\v 30 And I will \w shew\w* \w wonders\w* in the \w heavens\w* and in the \w earth\w*, \w blood\w*, and \w fire\w*, and \w pillars\w* of \w smoke\w*.  
\v 31 The \w sun\w* shall be \w turned\w* into \w darkness\w*, and the \w moon\w* into \w blood\w*, \w before\w* the \w great\w* and the \w terrible\w* \w day\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \w come\w*.  
\v 32 And it shall come to pass, \add that\add* whosoever shall \w call\w* on the \w name\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* shall be \w delivered\w*: for in \w mount\w* \w Zion\w* and in \w Jerusalem\w* shall be \w deliverance\w*, as the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* hath \w said\w*, and in the \w remnant\w* whom the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* shall \w call\w*.   
\c 3  
\p
\v 1 For, behold, in those \w days\w*, and in that \w time\w*, when I shall bring \w again\w* the \w captivity\w* of \w Judah\w* and \w Jerusalem\w*,  
\v 2 I will also \w gather\w* all \w nations\w*, and will bring them \w down\w* into the \w valley\w* of \w Jehoshaphat\w*, and will \w plead\w* with them there for my \w people\w* and \add for\add* my \w heritage\w* \w Israel\w*, whom they have \w scattered\w* among the \w nations\w*, and \w parted\w* my \w land\w*.  
\v 3 And they have \w cast\w* \w lots\w* for my \w people\w*; and have \w given\w* a \w boy\w* for an \w harlot\w*, and \w sold\w* a \w girl\w* for \w wine\w*, that they might \w drink\w*.  
\v 4 Yea, and what have ye to do with me, O \w Tyre\w*, and \w Zidon\w*, and all the \w coasts\w* of \w Palestine\w*? will ye \w render\w* me a \w recompence\w*? and if ye \w recompense\w* me, \w swiftly\w* \add and\add* \w speedily\w* will I \w return\w* your \w recompence\w* upon your own \w head\w*;  
\v 5 Because ye have \w taken\w* my \w silver\w* and my \w gold\w*, and have \w carried\w* into your \w temples\w* my \w goodly\w* pleasant \w things\w*:\f + \fr 3.5 \ft pleasant: Heb. desirable\f*  
\v 6 The \w children\w* also of \w Judah\w* and the \w children\w* of \w Jerusalem\w* have ye \w sold\w* unto the \w Grecians\w*, that ye might remove them \w far\w* from their \w border\w*.\f + \fr 3.6 \ft the Grecians: Heb. the sons of the Grecians\f*  
\v 7 Behold, I will \w raise\w* them out of the \w place\w* whither ye have \w sold\w* them, and will \w return\w* your \w recompence\w* upon your own \w head\w*:  
\v 8 And I will \w sell\w* your \w sons\w* and your \w daughters\w* into the \w hand\w* of the \w children\w* of \w Judah\w*, and they shall \w sell\w* them to the \w Sabeans\w*, to a \w people\w* far \w off\w*: for the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* hath \w spoken\w* \add it\add*.   
\p
\v 9 ¶ \w Proclaim\w* ye this among the \w Gentiles\w*; \w Prepare\w* \w war\w*, wake \w up\w* the mighty \w men\w*, let all the \w men\w* of \w war\w* draw \w near\w*; let them come \w up\w*:\f + \fr 3.9 \ft Prepare: Heb. Sanctify\f*  
\v 10 \w Beat\w* your \w plowshares\w* into \w swords\w*, and your \w pruninghooks\w* into \w spears\w*: let the \w weak\w* \w say\w*, I \add am\add* \w strong\w*.\f + \fr 3.10 \ft pruninghooks: or, scythes\f*  
\v 11 \w Assemble\w* yourselves, and \w come\w*, all ye \w heathen\w*, and gather yourselves \w together\w* round \w about\w*: thither cause thy mighty \w ones\w* to come \w down\w*, O \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*.\f + \fr 3.11 \ft cause…: or, the \+nd LORD\+nd* shall bring down\f*  
\v 12 Let the \w heathen\w* be \w wakened\w*, and come \w up\w* to the \w valley\w* of \w Jehoshaphat\w*: for there will I \w sit\w* to \w judge\w* all the \w heathen\w* round \w about\w*.  
\v 13 \w Put\w* ye in the \w sickle\w*, for the \w harvest\w* is \w ripe\w*: \w come\w*, get you \w down\w*; for the \w press\w* is \w full\w*, the \w fats\w* \w overflow\w*; for their \w wickedness\w* \add is\add* \w great\w*.  
\v 14 \w Multitudes\w*, \w multitudes\w* in the \w valley\w* of \w decision\w*: for the \w day\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \add is\add* \w near\w* in the \w valley\w* of \w decision\w*.\f + \fr 3.14 \ft decision: or, concision, or, threshing\f*  
\v 15 The \w sun\w* and the \w moon\w* shall be \w darkened\w*, and the \w stars\w* shall \w withdraw\w* their \w shining\w*.  
\v 16 The \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* also shall \w roar\w* out of \w Zion\w*, and \w utter\w* his \w voice\w* from \w Jerusalem\w*; and the \w heavens\w* and the \w earth\w* shall \w shake\w*: but the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \add will be\add* the \w hope\w* of his \w people\w*, and the \w strength\w* of the \w children\w* of \w Israel\w*.\f + \fr 3.16 \ft hope: Heb. place of repair, or, harbour\f*  
\v 17 So shall ye \w know\w* that I \add am\add* the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* your \w God\w* \w dwelling\w* in \w Zion\w*, my \w holy\w* \w mountain\w*: then shall \w Jerusalem\w* be \w holy\w*, and there shall no \w strangers\w* pass \w through\w* her any more.\f + \fr 3.17 \ft holy: Heb. holiness\f*   
\p
\v 18 ¶ And it shall come to pass in that \w day\w*, \add that\add* the \w mountains\w* shall drop \w down\w* new \w wine\w*, and the \w hills\w* shall \w flow\w* with \w milk\w*, and all the \w rivers\w* of \w Judah\w* shall \w flow\w* with \w waters\w*, and a \w fountain\w* shall come \w forth\w* of the \w house\w* of the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd*, and shall \w water\w* the \w valley\w* of \w Shittim\w*.\f + \fr 3.18 \ft flow: Heb. go\f*  
\v 19 \w Egypt\w* shall be a \w desolation\w*, and \w Edom\w* shall be a \w desolate\w* \w wilderness\w*, for the \w violence\w* \add against\add* the \w children\w* of \w Judah\w*, because they have \w shed\w* \w innocent\w* \w blood\w* in their \w land\w*.  
\v 20 But \w Judah\w* shall \w dwell\w* for \w ever\w*, and \w Jerusalem\w* from \w generation\w* to \w generation\w*.\f + \fr 3.20 \ft dwell: or, abide\f*  
\v 21 For I will \w cleanse\w* their \w blood\w* \add that\add* I have not \w cleansed\w*: for the \nd \+w LORD\+w*\nd* \w dwelleth\w* in \w Zion\w*.\f + \fr 3.21 \ft for the…: or, even I the \+nd LORD\+nd* that\f*
